            "Objects_ContentFormatting_FontSize": "Font size",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_FontSize_Description": "Thie default size to apply to the HTML body text font.\n\n\ud835\ude49\ud835\ude64\ud835\ude69\ud835\ude5a \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude29\ud835\ude22\ud835\ude35 \ud835\ude22\ud835\ude31\ud835\ude31\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude3a\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude28 \ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude26 \ud835\ude34\ud835\ude35\ud835\ude3a\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude34 \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude30 \ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2e\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude35\ud835\ude34 \ud835\ude2e\ud835\ude22\ud835\ude3a \ud835\ude30\ud835\ude37\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude33\ud835\ude33\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude25\ud835\ude26 \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude29\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude34.",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_FontColour": "Font color",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_FontColour_Description": "The default color to apply to the HTML body text.\n\n\ud835\ude49\ud835\ude64\ud835\ude69\ud835\ude5a \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude29\ud835\ude22\ud835\ude35 \ud835\ude22\ud835\ude31\ud835\ude31\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude3a\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude28 \ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude26 \ud835\ude34\ud835\ude35\ud835\ude3a\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude34 \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude30 \ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2e\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude35\ud835\ude34 \ud835\ude2e\ud835\ude22\ud835\ude3a \ud835\ude30\ud835\ude37\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude33\ud835\ude33\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude25\ud835\ude26 \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude29\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude34.",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_Align": "Text alignment",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_Alig_Description": "The default text alignment to apply to the the HTML Body.\n\n\ud835\ude49\ud835\ude64\ud835\ude69\ud835\ude5a \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude29\ud835\ude22\ud835\ude35 \ud835\ude22\ud835\ude31\ud835\ude31\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude3a\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude28 \ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude26 \ud835\ude34\ud835\ude35\ud835\ude3a\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude34 \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude30 \ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2d\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2e\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude2f\ud835\ude35\ud835\ude34 \ud835\ude2e\ud835\ude22\ud835\ude3a \ud835\ude30\ud835\ude37\ud835\ude26\ud835\ude33\ud835\ude33\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude25\ud835\ude26 \ud835\ude35\ud835\ude29\ud835\ude2a\ud835\ude34.",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_OverrideInlineStyling": "Override inline styling",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_OverrideInlineStyling_Description": "Force the four properties above (font family, font size, font color, text alignment) to apply to every element in the rendered HTML, even those carrying inline \ud835\ude9c\ud835\ude9d\ud835\udea2\ud835\ude95\ud835\ude8e attributes. Useful when content was pasted from Outlook, Teams, or Word and you want the visual's body styling to be authoritative.\n\nWhen disabled (default), inline color, font, and alignment are honored as authored \u2014 recommended when your data emits intentional inline styles (e.g., conditional formatting via DAX).\n\nThis setting has no effect when a \ud835\uddd6\ud835\ude02\ud835\ude00\ud835\ude01\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddfa \ud835\ude00\ud835\ude01\ud835\ude06\ud835\uddf9\ud835\uddf2\ud835\ude00\ud835\uddf5\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf2\ud835\ude01 is supplied; in that mode the stylesheet is the sole source of styling.",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_Hyperlinks": "Allow opening URLs",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_Hyperlinks_Description": "For security reasons, custom visuals cannot directly open hyperlinks that redirect to a URL.\n\nBy setting this option, the visual will \ud835\uddf1\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf9\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf4\ud835\uddee\ud835\ude01\ud835\uddf2 \ud835\ude01\ud835\uddf5\ud835\uddf2 \ud835\ude02\ud835\ude00\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddff'\ud835\ude00 \ud835\uddff\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddfe\ud835\ude02\ud835\uddf2\ud835\ude00\ud835\ude01 \ud835\ude01\ud835\uddfc \ud835\uddfb\ud835\uddee\ud835\ude03\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddf4\ud835\uddee\ud835\ude01\ud835\uddf2 \ud835\ude01\ud835\uddfc \ud835\uddee \ud835\udde8\ud835\udde5\ud835\udddf \ud835\ude01\ud835\uddfc \ud835\udde3\ud835\uddfc\ud835\ude04\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddff \ud835\uddd5\ud835\udddc, which if permitted, will prompt the user for their approval for any remote navigation.",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_UserSelect": "Allow text select",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_UserSelect_Description": "If enabled, you can use the mouse to select text within the visual container. You can copy this to the clipboard with Ctrl + C, or your operating system's default.",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_NoDataMessage": "\"No Data\" message",
            "Objects_ContentFormatting_NoDataMessage_Description": "If your visual contains no data, you are able to specify the message that is displayed. You can assign this a measure containing HTML using conditional formatting, if you so wish.",
            "Objects_Stylesheet": "Stylesheet",
            "Objects_Stylesheet_Description": "Here you can use conditional formatting to apply valid CSS for the entire visual's stylesheet using a measure with the desired content.",
            "Objects_Templates": "Templates",
            "Objects_Templates_Description": "Wrap and compose your content with HTML templates. Use the {{content}} token in the body template to mark where rows go, and the {{row}} token in the row template to mark where each row's value goes.",
            "Objects_Templates_BodyTemplate": "Body template",
            "Objects_Templates_BodyTemplate_Description": "HTML wrapped around all rows. The {{content}} token marks where the rendered rows are inserted. Supports conditional formatting from a measure.",
            "Objects_Templates_RowTemplate": "Row template",
            "Objects_Templates_RowTemplate_Description": "HTML wrapped around each row. The {{row}} token marks where the row's value goes. Vary the content per row from your measure; set this to {{row}} when your measure already emits the row element (e.g. a <tr> for a table).",
            "Objects_CrossFilter": "Cross-filtering",
            "Objects_CrossFilter_Description": "If enabled, this will invoke cross-filtering of other visuals, based on the Context of your dataset.",
            "Objects_CrossFilter_Enabled": "Enable",
            "Objects_CrossFilter_Enabled_Description": "Enable cross-filtering of other visuals, if Context is provided.",
            "Objects_CrossFilter_UseTransparency": "Set transparency of unselected items",
            "Objects_CrossFilter_UseTransparency_Description": "If enabled, this will set the use transparency to indicate non-selected items. Alternatively, you can manually set the styling of non-selected items by using the .\ud835\ude91\ud835\ude9d\ud835\ude96\ud835\ude95\ud835\ude85\ud835\ude92\ud835\ude8e\ud835\udea0\ud835\ude8e\ud835\ude9b\ud835\ude74\ud835\ude97\ud835\ude9d\ud835\ude9b\ud835\udea2.\ud835\ude9e\ud835\ude97\ud835\ude9c\ud835\ude8e\ud835\ude95\ud835\ude8e\ud835\ude8c\ud835\ude9d\ud835\ude8e\ud835\ude8d CSS class in your stylesheet.",
            "Objects_CrossFilter_TransparencyPercent": "Transparency",
            "Objects_CrossFilter_TransparencyPercent_Description": "The transparency percentage to apply to unselected items.",
            "Objects_Compatibility": "Compatibility",
            "Objects_Compatibility_Description": "Compatibility options for reports built with earlier versions of the visual.",
            "Objects_Compatibility_LegacyRendering": "Use legacy (v1) rendering",
            "Objects_Compatibility_LegacyRendering_Description": "Render content with the v1 styling rules and row structure. Turned on automatically for reports migrated from v1; off for new visuals.",
